.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH config 1  "config " 
.SH NAME
config \- Read and write the local configuration (registry, colour, shell, default visibility, cache size). No secrets: tokens stay in the credential store
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBconfig\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read and write the local configuration (registry, colour, shell, default visibility, cache size). No secrets: tokens stay in the credential store
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
config\-list(1)
List every config key with its effective value and source
.TP
config\-get(1)
Print one key\*(Aqs effective value
.TP
config\-set(1)
Validate and save one key\*(Aqs value
.TP
config\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg config list
  fg config get color
  fg config set color never
  fg config set registry_url https://forgehub.example
